## Exact edit prompt

```text
Use case: precise-object-edit.
Asset type: ONE transparent pixel 2.5D game-enemy cutout, Cinder Act 3 Sunbound Stalker C50 / A3-E1, FRONT ALPPAIN SETTLED RECOVERY candidate.

Input 1, sunbound-stalker-recovery.png, is the EXACT EDIT TARGET and authoritative body identity, LOW SETTLED pose, anatomy, facing, native scale, placement, palette and feet reference.
Input 2, sunbound-stalker-alppain-readable.png, is SUPPORT ONLY for the SAME SHORT BROAD OPEN TWO-PRONG HEAD CREST in the Alppain configuration. Do not copy its taller braced body or leg pose.

Primary request: keep Input 1's settled recovery creature unchanged outside the HEAD CREST. Change ONLY its existing directional head crest at the lowered lower-right-facing head into the same short substantial angular two-prong fork configuration as Input 2. The prongs must frame a genuinely transparent open V/U-shaped gap, at least 58 native pixels wide at its widest part, preferably around 60–90 native pixels on this 1254-square canvas. It should stay as a broad clear opening at small portrait scale, not close into a painted dark stripe or microglint. Keep the fork SHORT and broad, not tall; it is the same existing organic crest reshaped, not a new horn, antenna, organ, crown, target or equipment. Maintain the lowered head/jaw and the same lower-right direction. Preserve the original back/dorsal plates rather than making their outline a fork.

Pose/body invariants: preserve Input 1's LOW, SETTLED, STATIONARY recovery pose exactly as faithfully as possible. Torso stays lowered with deeply bent bracing limbs; do not lift it into Input 2's preparation stance. Keep all FOUR existing angular limbs, every planted clawed foot, negative-space limb gaps, original body proportions, same nearby open low flank and its restrained pale ivory/muted-lime plate join. Do not turn or translate the organism, replace its head, redraw the body, shorten the upper back, alter feet, add appendages or invent new anatomy. The low seam remains the same anatomical plate join, without glow or a separate symbol.

View/style: same approximately 45-degree overhead orthographic three-quarter lower-right-facing pixel 2.5D interpretation as Input 1. Preserve its violet/lavender/black-purple organic plate family, crisp stepped pixel contours, broad flat facets and restrained glassy highlights. Keep a few broad value planes; no additional sparkly microglints, neon outline, bloom, painterly texture or smooth rendered replacement.

Canvas/scale/pivot invariants: preserve the 1254-by-1254 transparent canvas and Input 1's full organism placement and native size. Keep the original upper body near its y416 visible top and the lowest planted feet baseline at y1060, with proposed feet pivot (635,1060) and source offset (-8,433). Do not crop, resize, zoom, rotate, recenter or renormalize the body. All four feet and transparent margins remain visible. Common family scale is 1.35/807 world units per native pixel; the lower recovery body must remain visibly lower at that unchanged scale.

Background: genuinely transparent alpha only, preserve transparency. No floor, ground plane, contact disk, shadow, geometry, scenery or backdrop.

Constraints: exactly one whole existing organism and one stationary recovery still. No duplicate, atlas, frame strip, other facing, active attack, lunge, motion trail, ray, laser, projectile, warning footprint, arrows, target gem, eye symbol, glow cue, equipment, weapon, pickup, UI, text, labels or watermark. Same C50/A3-E1 enemy and same Alppain crest configuration; original game art, not novel canon. This image defines no new enemy/ability, exclusive flank, damage, collision, phase duration, vulnerability or mechanic. Change only the existing head crest to the supported short broad open fork while preserving the exact settled recovery identity, pose and feet placement.
```


